BUILD INPUTS, NOT REDISTRIBUTED

  Linux kernel headers, the kernel build system, and the DRM helpers
  exported by the kernel (including those exported with
  EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL)
    Licence:   GPL-2.0-only (the kernel as a whole, per its COPYING
               file). The Linux-syscall-note exception applies to the
               kernel's uapi headers only, and not to these modules.
               Individual kernel files carry their own SPDX identifiers.
    Copyright: the Linux kernel's many copyright holders, as recorded in
               the kernel source
    Source:    https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git

  The modules are compiled against the headers and build system of the
  kernel they will run on: the guest's own installed kernel headers when
  built through DKMS, and each distribution's own kernel headers in CI.
  No copy of any kernel file is placed in this repository or shipped from
  it, so no notice obligation arises from those files.

  The obligation that does arise is on the modules themselves. They must
  declare a GPL-compatible licence to resolve symbols exported with
  EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL, they are distributed under GPL-2.0-only, and
  distributing them under GPL-2.0-only requires distributing their
  complete corresponding source, including the build and install scripts.
  README.md lists what that includes.

  The Linux-syscall-note exception (SPDX: Linux-syscall-note), which the
  kernel applies to its uapi headers, says that user programs using
  kernel services by normal system calls are not derived works of the
  kernel. It covers userspace programs that use the kernel's uapi. It
  does not cover kernel modules, and nothing in this repository relies on
  it.


